From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:50:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: butterfly and moth netting, their Hunters' Rumours

Catching butterflies and moths (wiki): a wielded butterfly net or magic
butterfly net, or barehanded at 10 levels above the requirement; the OSRS
256 roll with the wiki's skilling success charts (black warlock, sunlight
and moonlight moths; the other butterflies copy the black warlock). A
butterfly jar keeps the catch; without one it is released and its effect
applies. Jarred butterflies get their Release op (Attack/Defence/Strength
boosts, Hitpoints, the sunlight moth's restore, the moonlight moth's
prayer). Catches count for Hunters' Rumours: sapphire glacialis, snowy
knight, black warlock, sunlight and moonlight moths are now assignable
(1/40, pity 80). The rare-part message uses the wiki's colour (#229628).
Data in dbtable hunter_butterflies; integration tests for the item moves.
